1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,070
Listen to a talk on an art podcast.

2
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:07,552
Today, we'll dive into the world of cubism,

3
00:00:07,552 --> 00:00:13,210
an innovative art movement that revolutionized the way we perceive and represent reality.

4
00:00:13,210 --> 00:00:16,920
Cubism emerged in the early 20th century

5
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:21,070
spearheaded by artists like Pablo Picasso and Georges Braque.

6
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:26,060
Unlike traditional art, which aimed to depict subjects from a single viewpoint

7
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:29,827
cubism fragmented objects into geometric shapes

8
00:00:29,827 --> 00:00:32,259
and presented multiple angles simultaneously.

9
00:00:32,259 --> 00:00:34,621
This technique challenged conventional perspectives

10
00:00:34,621 --> 00:00:40,290
and provided a more dynamic and complex representation of the subject matter.

11
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:49,290
One of the most iconic works of cubism is Picasso's painting "Les Demoiselles d'Avignon," or "The Young Ladies of Avignon" in English.

12
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:57,040
It was revolutionary, breaking away from realism with distorted figures and jagged geometric shapes.

13
00:00:57,040 --> 00:01:02,060
It rejected the traditional perspective, presenting multiple viewpoints at once.

14
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:06,250
And the painting shocked audiences with its raw, fragmented forms.

15
00:01:06,250 --> 00:01:12,240
Cubism can be divided into two phases: Analytical Cubism and Synthetic Cubism.

16
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:17,221
Analytical Cubism focused on deconstructing objects into basic geometric forms

17
00:01:17,221 --> 00:01:23,199
and muted colors while Synthetic Cubism introduced brighter colors and collage techniques,

18
00:01:23,199 --> 00:01:28,180
integrating different materials like newspapers and fabric into the artwork.

19
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:32,160
The impact of cubism extended beyond the visual arts

20
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:36,000
influencing literature, architecture and even music.

21
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,391
Its emphasis on abstraction and multiplicity of perspectives inspired artists

22
00:01:40,391 --> 00:01:46,100
and thinkers to explore new ways of expressing ideas and interpreting the world.

23
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:50,276
Ultimately, cubism paved the way for many modern art movements,

24
00:01:50,276 --> 00:01:53,200
leaving a lasting legacy on artistic expression.
